 /// its final pending frame must still be delivered after the source goes quiet.
+///
+/// Emissions follow an ideal cadence: each one takes the slot after the
+/// previous one, not the moment the timer actually fired, so timer lateness
+/// does not accumulate into a lower frame rate. A stream that has fallen a
+/// whole interval behind restarts its cadence instead of bursting to catch up.
+///
+/// A repeating stream re-sends its latest frame while the source is quiet.
+/// With `settleRepeats` it stops after that many repeats; `settled` marks the
+/// final repeat so an encoder can finish on a clean frame.
